# Plan ARIA-V2 §3.4 — full per-clone runtime state sweep (Phase 5).
# GDPR rationale: ARIA_ACTOR defaults to <user>@<hostname> (personal
# data per GDPR Art 4); operator --reason text is free-text PII-
# adjacent. Storing the runtime ledgers only on the operator's
# machine is data-minimization-correct, and the committed daily
# anchor (Phase 6) replaces git history as the audit-trust source.
# Tracked allowlist enforced by aria-kernel/tests/test_aria_tools_tracked_allowlist.py (I-23):
#   - aria-tools/repo_identity.json     (v3 schema stamp, version fields only)
#   - aria-tools/agent-evals/fixtures/   (eval fixtures)
#   - aria-tools/reports/daily/          (daily chain-tip anchors, Phase 6)
aria-tools/registry.json
aria-tools/registry-stub-allowlist.json
aria-tools/agent-invocations/
aria-tools/agent-network/
aria-tools/capability-gaps/
aria-tools/change-ledger/
aria-tools/cycle-diff/
aria-tools/cycle-state/
aria-tools/cycle-metrics/
aria-tools/dashboards/
aria-tools/discovery/
aria-tools/dispatch/
aria-tools/fitness/
aria-tools/memory/
aria-tools/observability/
aria-tools/plans/
aria-tools/pressure/
